      "value": "@{5a95256f54d514123c1f089d|full_name}: From my understanding, the OP is the world creator since they included the following, along with all the Unity and SDK information: As a conjecture, I think that it occurs when I use Japanese (multi-byte) in the hierarchy of the scene of Unity.\nSo I don't think it's necessarily the \"map creator's\" fault. The game should be able to support these interactions. From what I understand, if they name an object りんごボックス, it breaks on the Quest. However, if they name the object \"Apple Box\", it works. This is the problem that has been observed.",
